I guess the real trouble with pudding farming is that it is terribly
boring.
And in Nethack getting bored is the way to get killed.
So pudding farming is actually a way to kill a promising character.

The only people who can do pudding farming successfully are very
careful players.
A careful player doesn't need pudding farming.

The inexperienced players never know when to stop. They stop only when
they die.
Experienced players recognize this strategy to be bad and won't use it.

So you will usually find that only conduct players use this strategy
successfully.
The rest would normally die. I would like to see a YAFAP which was done
using
pudding farming. I am sure this will not happen.

So pudding farming cannot be called unbalancing, it can only be called
a death trap.

